lgx-runtime (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bug fixes and improvements:
    - Fixed ISO C pedantic compliance in namespace isolation
    - Eliminated variable length arrays (VLA) in test code for better portability
    - Added NULL safety checks in test code
    - Suppressed intentional NULL dereference warnings in signal handling tests
    - Fixed stack protector warnings across test suite
  * New features:
    - Added comprehensive benchmark suite (5 benchmarks)
    - Benchmark framework with statistical analysis
    - Performance measurement tools for allocation, memory patterns, hardware adaptation
  * Security improvements:
    - All code passes strict GCC static analysis with -fanalyzer
    - Zero warnings with -Wpedantic -Werror
    - Enhanced code quality and ISO C compliance
  * Build improvements:
    - All 59 tests compile cleanly
    - All 5 benchmarks compile cleanly
    - Zero compilation warnings in release builds

 -- LGX Platform Team <team@lgx-platform.org>  Thu, 12 Feb 2026 23:10:00 +0100

lgx-runtime (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of LGX Runtime Core
  * Features:
    - Ultra-fast frame arena allocator (P99 < 100ns)
    - GPU memory pool with Vulkan integration
    - Persistent heap allocator with low fragmentation
    - Intent-based allocation API for automatic routing
    - Hardware adaptation and graceful degradation
    - Privacy-first telemetry framework
    - Comprehensive error handling and observability
  * Performance achievements:
    - Allocation latency: P99 = 84ns (frame arena)
    - Memory overhead: 1.03 MB (199x under target)
    - Initialization time: 2.70 ms (185x faster than target)
  * Supported distributions:
    - Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (Jammy Jellyfish)
    - Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (Noble Numbat)
    - Debian 11 (Bullseye)
    - Debian 12 (Bookworm)

 -- LGX Platform Team <team@lgx-platform.org>  Mon, 09 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
